1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:08,840
When talking about proteins you usually think of food such as meat and egg-

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,320
-But rarely do we talk about the thousands of proteins that build our bodies.

3
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:19,760
Without them we would not exist.

4
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:29,240
There are several thousand protein in the body.

5
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:35,760
They are called the body's building blocks as they build up bones, tissues and muscles-

6
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:40,600
-But even hormones, enzymes and antibodies are proteins.

7
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:43,040
They are found everywhere in the body-

8
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,840
-And is of great importance for the body's functions and structure.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,440
The proteins are produced in the body's cells, more specifically the ribosomes-

10
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,200
-cellen's small factories.

11
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:32,280
The protein gets specific properties-

12
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:38,200
-Dore depending on which amino acids are involved and their order.

13
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:42,800
The combinations are almost endless.

14
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:49,560
When the chain is done, it is folded together and the protein gets its unique structure.

15
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:55,320
In order for protein to be formed, the amino acids must be found in our bodies.

16
00:01:55,480 --> 00:02:02,240
We cannot make all ourselves.
We get nine pieces through the food.

17
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:07,320
In the past, it was believed that proteins were unique to a specific tissue.

18
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:11,760
That they were just there.
But that theory is littered.

19
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:18,360
Today we know that a protein in the knee joint may be in your gut.

20
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:25,040
Proteins are not just building materials in tissues, muscles and bones.

21
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:31,480
They are much more than that and are behind many chemical processes.

22
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:37,160
Enzymes, receptors, hormones and antibodies are all protein-

23
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:42,120
-And has a role in our cell communication and interaction.

24
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:48,640
Hormones are formed in glands and transported to different organ-

25
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,760
-Where they affect different cells.

26
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:57,920
Receptors are protein that captures external signals-

27
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:00,800
-And sends them into the cell.

28
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:05,720
Antibodies Flag marks intruders in the body-

29
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:10,080
-and calls on the immune system's killer cells-
